From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:57:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sf: e-ink: drop the legacy enhancement pass
 (debug.sf.eink_render=2)

Only reachable with debug.sf.eink_render below 3 (system.prop sets 3), and no
tool uses it any more. Removed: kEinkEnhanceSkSL and drawEinkEnhance, the
solid1/solid2/black/white settings with debug.sf.eink_enhance.fast,
.solid1_x1000, .solid2_x1000 and vendor.xrz.hibreak_contrast_black/white, and
the matching branch in getEinkEnhance and einkDamagePadding. The render pass
keeps radius, t1, t2, gate0, gate1 and the strength. With debug.sf.eink_render
below 3 there is now no pass, where it ran the old one.

Checked without a build: getEinkEnhance and einkDamagePadding give the same
results as before over 900,000 random property sequences with the render pass
on or enhance at 0, and no pass below 3; the old and the new code compile with
-Wall -Wextra -Werror against stub headers; DisplaySettings.h compiles and no
longer accepts the removed fields.
